<title>CANADA: Canada W. coast ship moves unhampered by blizzard.</title>
<headline>Canada W. coast ship moves unhampered by blizzard.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo ship movements in and out of western Canada's port of Vancouver were not hampered by Sunday's blizzard on British Columbia's coast, a Canadian Wheat Board spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;There's no disruptions in Vancouver because of the weather,&quot; CWB spokesman Jim Pietryk said.</p>
<p>The blizzard dumped 34 cms (13.5 inches) of snow on Vancouver in the 24-hour period ended Sunday evening.</p>
<p>((--Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
